Dataset Name:
Used Cars - Uncovering Factors That Affect Used Car Prices


Dataset Source(s):
Main Source - https://data.world/data-society/used-cars-data


Dataset Authors:
@Data-Society - (Original Owners)


Description:
This dataset contains information on used car listings (scraped with a bot) in 
Germany over many years, including variables such as price, year of registration,
mileage (kilometers driven), and engine power. The data represents real-world 
vehicle listings and allows for analysis of factors that influence car prices.


Side Note:
Since this dataset has German origin, the author has made sure that all variables are
in english BUT the actual data may not be. This is fine since after a data clean we are
left with majority numerical and universal variables so no translationis needed. If there
is a translation it would be for the categorical variables.

Examples:

Response variable (Y):
- price


Main Explanatory Variables (X):
- yearOfRegistration (Quantitive)
- powerPS (Quantitive)
- kilometer (Quantitive)


Optional Explanatory Variables (X):
- seller (Categorical)
- vehicleType (Categorical)
- gearbox (Categorical)
- fuelType (Categorical)
- brand (?) <- might remove since there are too many!
- notRepairDamage (Categorical)


Purpose of the Study:
The main purpose is to figure out exactly what factors affect used car prices. Basically if
we know variables like car's year, mileage, power, etc, how well can we predict its price?
With this model we can hopefully get a brief explanation of car prices (generally worldwide)
using data.


